  "items": [
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "Israeli attacks across the Gaza Strip kill at least 72 more Palestinians as the assault to capture Gaza City continues. ((Al Jazeera))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "Israel carries out a series of airstrikes against alleged Houthi targets and civilian structures in Sanaa and Al Jawf Governorate, Yemen, killing 35 people and wounding 131 others. ((Al Jazeera))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "The Polish Air Force and NATO allies scramble fighter jets in response to 19 Russian drones penetrating up to 250 km into Polish airspace during an overnight air attack on Ukraine. ((BBC News))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "The Polish Armed Forces confirms it has shot down four Russian drones over the country, marking the first time Poland has directly engaged Russian military assets since the start of the war. ((BBC News))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "Poland closes multiple airports due to the airspace breach, including Warsaw Modlin Airport, Rzeszów–Jasionka Airport, and Lublin Airport. ((CNN))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "Polish prime minister Donald Tusk invokes Article 4 of the North Atlantic Treaty following the incursion. ((The Guardian))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "Nepal deploys its military to enforce an indefinite curfew in Kathmandu following anti-corruption protests. ((Euronews))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "Kathmandu's Tribhuvan International Airport reopens nearly a day after the Nepali Army occupied it. ((BBC News))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Armed conflicts and attacks",
      "text": "American right-wing political activist Charlie Kirk is shot dead during a debate at Utah Valley University in Orem, Utah, United States. ((The Guardian))"
    },
    {
      "category": "Disasters and accidents",
      "text": "Cuba experiences its fifth nationwide power outage in less than a year, affecting about 10 million people. ((The Guardian))"
    },
    {
